  "body": "`edit.BlockList` (internal/edit/yaml.go) turns a flow-style list into block style for both dsh patch-list parsers (`dshParse` in internal/agent/dsh.go, `dshRead` in internal/library/dsh.go). yaml.v3 accepts a root flow sequence followed by block content, and BlockList keeps only the flow sequence, so the lines after it are dropped when magpie writes the file back.\n\nFound while reviewing #2667, on origin/main 7660399a1 (not changed by that fix):\n\n```\nBlockList(\"[]\\n- id: a\\n\")              -> \"[]\\n\", true\nBlockList(\"[ {id: x} ]\\n- id: a\\n\")     -> \"- id: x\\n\", true\nBlockList(\"--- []\\n- id: a\\n\")          -> \"[]\\n\", true\nBlockList(\"--- [ {id: x} ]\\n\")          -> \"- id: x\\n\", true   (the marker is dropped too)\n```\n\nSuch a file isn't valid YAML for dsh either, but magpie should refuse it (\"not a list of entries magpie can edit\") rather than delete the user's `- id: a` entry. A fix could check that nothing but comments/blank lines follows the sequence's end line before returning ok, and keep a `---` that shares the sequence's line.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
